cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "psimodpy: A Python library for the PSI-MOD protein modification ontology"
abstract: >-
  psimodpy is a typed Python package for parsing and querying the PSI-MOD
  protein modification ontology. It ships with the bundled PSI-MOD OBO data
  so it works offline, parses OBO source files into structured PsiModEntry
  objects covering terms, synonyms, cross-references, relationships, and
  formula/mass annotations, and exposes a queryable in-memory database with
  TSV/CSV export and a round-trip OBO writer. An optional FastAPI and Model
  Context Protocol server exposes the same database over HTTP for
  interactive lookups and integration with proteomics tooling. psimodpy is
  intended for proteomics software, annotation pipelines, and research
  scripts that need programmatic access to PSI-MOD terms. It requires
  Python 3.12 or later.
